 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 505 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Tuckahoe, in relation\nto extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6712",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6712-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 505 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6712\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 505 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Tucka-\nhoe, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo extend the expiration date of chapter 505 of the laws of 2016, which\nauthorizes the Village of Tuckahoe to enact a room occupancy tax not to\nexceed 3%.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section 1. Extends the authority of the Village of Tuckahoe to enact a\nroom occupancy tax not exceeding 3%, as authorized by chapter 505 of the\nlaws of 2016, to September 1, 2027.\n\n  Section 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter  505  of  the  laws  of 2016 granted the Village of Tuckahoe the\nability to impose a 3% daily room tax on any room in a hotel, motel,  or\nsimilar  place of public accommodation. This tax has helped raise reven-\nues to support municipal expenses. The law is set to expire on September\n1, 2025 and this legislation will extend the expiration date to  Septem-\nber 1, 2027.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: S8042/A9089; L2022, ch.409\n\n2019: S5082/A6473; L2019, ch.210\n\n2016: S7153/A9690; L 2016, ch. 505\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
